# Stale pre-multiversion copy of the project. The live source tree is root src/.
# This folder is a near-identical duplicate and must never be committed from here.
AJ Tools/

# The installer ships from its own separate GitHub repository
# (Ajmalpshaik/AJ-Tools-Installer) and carries its own .git.
AJ-Tools-Installer/

# Claude working folder: everything is backed up EXCEPT machine-local state.
# settings.local.json is per-machine by design and scheduled_tasks.lock is runtime state -
# both would only create noise between machines. The knowledge, skills, scripts and
# scratch folders ARE tracked on purpose; they are the accumulated working memory.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# The Codex working folder, for the same reason settings.local.json is ignored
# above: it is MACHINE-LOCAL STATE, not project content. Both files in it name
# an absolute path on one PC - a pinned node build under Documents, this repo's
# own D: location, and a tool's exe under a user profile. Published to a public
# repository that leaks a directory layout and works on nobody else's machine,
# including this one after a reinstall.
#
# The sibling project tracks its equivalent because its config is PORTABLE -
# `command = "python"`, a relative path, nothing about a particular PC. If this
# one is ever rewritten that way it can be tracked too; until then it is noise
# between machines, which is exactly what the rule above exists for.
.codex/

# A separate product used to live under this root and was moved out to its own repository.
# Two copies of anything drift apart, which has already cost real time here once with the old
# "AJ Tools\" tree. If one of these folders reappears under this root it is a stale copy, not work.
connector/
connector-tools/
